# JavaScript Code to Remove Age Pattern

Here are several approaches to remove "(age X)" from your string:

## 1. **Using Regular Expression (Recommended)**

```javascript
const str = "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";
const result = str.replace(/\s*\(age\s+\d+\)/g, "");
console.log(result);
// Output: "july 7 1994 London, UK (1994-07-07)"
```

## 2. **Remove Only First Occurrence**

```javascript
const str = "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";
const result = str.replace(/\s*\(age\s+\d+\)/, "");
console.log(result);
// Output: "july 7 1994 London, UK (1994-07-07)"
```

## 3. **Case-Insensitive Removal**

```javascript
const str = "july 7 1994 (Age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";
const result = str.replace(/\s*\(age\s+\d+\)/gi, "");
console.log(result);
// Output: "july 7 1994 London, UK (1994-07-07)"
```

## 4. **Reusable Function**

```javascript
function removeAge(str) {
  return str.replace(/\s*\(age\s+\d+\)/gi, "");
}

const str = "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";
console.log(removeAge(str));
// Output: "july 7 1994 London, UK (1994-07-07)"
```

## 5. **With Trim to Remove Extra Spaces**

```javascript
function removeAge(str) {
  return str.replace(/\s*\(age\s+\d+\)\s*/gi, " ").trim();
}

const str = "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";
console.log(removeAge(str));
```

---

## **Regex Explanation:**
- `\s*` - Zero or more whitespace characters
- `\(age` - Literal "(age" text
- `\s+` - One or more whitespace characters
- `\d+` - One or more digits
- `\)` - Literal ")" character
- `g` - Global flag (all occurrences)
- `i` - Case-insensitive flag

**Choose option #1 or #4** for most use cases! 🎯

